  m_Name: C
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  attachedPhoto: {fileID: 0}
  logText: The capsule containing this species has detailed information about them.
    Their name can be translated to Povann. They were an advanced underwater civilization
    that lived all over the oceans of the planet. They had two long tentacle legs
    with fins for movement, as well as two smaller ones that they used like arms.
    The tip of the small ones has many tiny fingers, comparable to the tentacles
    of a jellyfish. There is a mouth at the bottom, used mainly for eating, and another
    one on the side of their body, used exclusively to communicate. The Povann had
    a set of grills at the top of their heads and one large eye on each side. Interior
    scans of their organs show two hearts, each helping pump blood to one of their
    long legs. The brain rests at the bottom of their body, between the mouths and
    the hearts. They have a simple, hardened skeleton used to protect their vital
    organs, accompanied by cartilage covering most of the body.  I should take all
    this information back to the ship for further investigation. Although I wish
    I could take the body with me.
  orderFound: 0
